+HarmonyOS Build Configuration for aom 3.9.1
+============================================
+
+1. CMake Configuration
+----------------------
+CMake does not recognize HarmonyOS platform, use Linux as workaround:
+  -DCMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=Linux
+  -DCMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR=aarch64
+  -DAOM_TARGET_CPU=generic  (disable assembly optimizations)
+
+2. Compiler Settings
+--------------------
+  -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=/data/service/hnp/bin/clang
+  -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=/data/service/hnp/bin/clang++
+  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
+
+3. Disable Components
+---------------------
+  -DENABLE_TESTS=OFF
+  -DENABLE_EXAMPLES=OFF  
+  -DENABLE_DOCS=OFF
+
+4. Build Options
+----------------
+For static library: Default build
+For shared library: -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON
+
+5. Installation
+---------------
+Install prefix: /usr/local (relative path for DESTDIR staging)
+DESTDIR for staging: /storage/Users/currentUser/tmpexport/test-install-aom-{version}
+
+6. Known Issues
+---------------
+- Assembly optimizations disabled (AOM_TARGET_CPU=generic)
+- No native HarmonyOS platform support in CMake
+- Build directory must be separate from source (CMake requirement)